WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.568 --> 00:00:20.133
Nothing could bring back my dear friend Helen, who had died so young from tuberculosis.

2
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:27.568
But after her death and the terrible typhus outbreak, an investigation was launched into conditions at Lowood.

3
00:00:27.569 --> 00:00:39.121
The unhealthy nature of the site, the poor quality of the food and water, the wretchedness of the girls' clothing and accommodations: all these things were discovered and deplored.

4
00:00:39.122 --> 00:00:47.288
Several wealthy individuals contributed money to improve the school, and Mr. Brocklehurst was stripped of most of his authority.

5
00:00:47.289 --> 00:00:58.697
In time Lowood became a truly useful and noble institution. I remained there for eight years, six as a student and two as a teacher.

6
00:00:58.698 --> 00:01:09.597
Through all the changes at Lowood, Miss Temple continued as superintendent. In my life she had taken the place of mother, governess, and friend.

7
00:01:09.598 --> 00:01:16.390
However, when I was 18, she married a clergyman and moved to a distant county.

8
00:01:16.391 --> 00:01:19.966
From the day she left, I was no longer the same.

9
00:01:19.966 --> 00:01:29.341
I'd absorbed from Miss Temple something of her nature and much of her habits. I was quiet, and I believed I was content.

10
00:01:29.342 --> 00:01:36.093
But as soon as her carriage departed after the wedding, I began to feel the stirring of old emotions.

11
00:01:36.094 --> 00:01:41.329
Up in my room, I went to my window and looked out at the hilly horizon.

12
00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:49.496
I traced the winding road until it vanished between two mountains. How I longed to follow it farther!

13
00:01:49.497 --> 00:01:54.089
"Let me be useful elsewhere!" I cried in desperation.

14
00:01:54.090 --> 00:02:00.396
Just then a bell called me to supper, and I was not free to resume my thoughts until bedtime.

15
00:02:00.397 --> 00:02:05.299
"What do I want?" I asked myself as I sat up in bed.

16
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:17.813
And then I knew. "I'd like a new position in a new house. How do people get new positions? They ask friends, I suppose, but I have no friends."

17
00:02:17.814 --> 00:02:28.791
Agitated from thinking so hard, I got up and paced the room. When I lay down again, the answer came to me: I must advertise in the newspaper.

18
00:02:28.792 --> 00:02:35.427
Before the bell rang the next morning, I had my advertisement written. It read as follows:

19
00:02:35.428 --> 00:02:41.035
"A young lady accustomed to teaching desires employment in a family with young children.

20
00:02:41.036 --> 00:02:51.189
She is qualified to teach the usual subjects plus French, drawing, and music. Reply to J.E., Post Office, Lowton."

21
00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:57.855
After tea I walked the two miles to Lowton and discreetly took my letter to the post office.

22
00:02:57.856 --> 00:03:01.597
I waited a week before I checked for a response.

23
00:03:01.598 --> 00:03:07.523
"Are there any letters for J.E.?" I anxiously asked the postmistress.

24
00:03:07.524 --> 00:03:16.509
She peered at me over her spectacles, and then she opened a drawer and fumbled among its contents for so long that I began to lose hope.

25
00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:20.357
At last she pushed an envelope across the counter.

26
00:03:20.358 --> 00:03:23.985
Outside the post office, I tore open the letter.

27
00:03:23.986 --> 00:03:35.372
It was from a Mrs. Fairfax of Thornfield near Millcote, and it offered a position teaching a little girl under ten years of age for the salary of thirty pounds per year.

28
00:03:35.372 --> 00:03:42.156
If I wanted the job, I should send my name, address, and letter of reference to Mrs. Fairfax.

29
00:03:42.157 --> 00:03:52.809
I studied the letter a long time. The writing was old fashioned, and I pictured Mrs. Fairfax as a model of elderly English respectability.

30
00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:58.658
Thornfield was doubtless the name of her house, a neat and orderly spot I was sure.

31
00:03:58.659 --> 00:04:05.306
I knew that Millcote was a large manufacturing town, seventy miles nearer London than Lowood.

32
00:04:05.307 --> 00:04:12.297
The next day I spoke to the superintendent at Lowood school about my opportunity and the letter of reference.

33
00:04:12.298 --> 00:04:19.543
She contacted Mr. Brocklehurst, who said that Mrs. Reed must be written to because she was my guardian.

34
00:04:19.544 --> 00:04:26.432
Mrs. Reed replied that I might do as I pleased as she'd long ago given up caring what I did.

35
00:04:26.433 --> 00:04:32.209
The school provided me with a reference, and Mrs. Fairfax offered me the position.

36
00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:39.120
I now busied myself preparing to leave Lowood. On my last day I packed my trunk.

37
00:04:39.121 --> 00:04:46.833
In half an hour, the carrier was to take it to Lowton, where I was to meet the coach early the next morning.

38
00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:51.180
I was too excited to sit still, so I paced the halls.

39
00:04:51.181 --> 00:04:56.994
"Miss," said a servant who encountered me, "someone wants to see you downstairs."

40
00:04:56.995 --> 00:05:03.908
I hurried downstairs, and as I passed the back parlor, a woman ran out and clasped my hand.

41
00:05:03.909 --> 00:05:07.906
"Jane! I'd know you anywhere!"

42
00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:12.275
I studied the woman, who appeared to be a well-dressed servant.

43
00:05:12.276 --> 00:05:15.659
"Bessie!" I cried as I embraced her.

44
00:05:15.659 --> 00:05:24.071
We went into the parlor, where she explained that when my letter arrived at Gateshead, she had vowed to see me one last time.

45
00:05:24.072 --> 00:05:28.897
"Tell me everything about everyone at Gateshead," I implored her.

46
00:05:28.898 --> 00:05:36.553
"Miss Eliza is much taller than you are," Bessie began, "and Miss Georgiana is very handsome.

47
00:05:36.554 --> 00:05:43.959
You look like a lady, and I suppose that's all we can expect. You were no beauty as a child."

48
00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:49.800
I smiled at her frankness. "I suppose Georgiana is very pretty?"

49
00:05:49.801 --> 00:05:55.877
"Oh yes. She went to London last winter and everyone admired her.

50
00:05:55.878 --> 00:06:04.211
A nobleman fell in love with her, but his family was against the match, so he and Miss Georgiana decided to run away.

51
00:06:04.212 --> 00:06:11.194
But Miss Eliza found out and they were stopped. Now the young ladies fight like cats and dogs."

52
00:06:11.195 --> 00:06:14.706
"And what of John Reed?" I asked.

53
00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:23.436
"He was sent home from college for failing his classes. His mother is always worried about him because he spends too much money.

54
00:06:23.437 --> 00:06:28.005
Now tell me about yourself. Can you play the piano?"

55
00:06:28.006 --> 00:06:33.670
There was one in the room, so I played a waltz or two and she was charmed.

56
00:06:33.671 --> 00:06:36.418
"Can you draw?" she asked.

57
00:06:36.419 --> 00:06:42.171
I pointed to one of my paintings over the fireplace, and Bessie was impressed.

58
00:06:42.172 --> 00:06:48.492
Then she asked if I'd ever heard anything from my Eyre relatives. I had not.

59
00:06:48.493 --> 00:06:55.565
I was stunned when she told me that a Mr. Eyre had come looking for me at Gateshead seven years ago.

60
00:06:55.566 --> 00:07:00.079
Mrs. Reed told him that I was at school fifty miles away.

61
00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:05.990
A wine merchant on his way to Madeira, Mr. Eyre did not have time to find me.

62
00:07:05.991 --> 00:07:15.157
Bessie and I talked of old times for another hour, but I kept thinking of how Mrs. Reed had never written to me about Mr. Eyre.

63
00:07:15.158 --> 00:07:22.141
The next morning I saw Bessie again for a few minutes as we waited for our respective coaches in Lowton.

64
00:07:22.142 --> 00:07:29.897
Then I climbed into the vehicle that was to carry me to my new life in a strange place.
